  "releaseNotes": "## AgentOS Core 2.0.0-beta.65\n\n- Adds per-Agent MCP tool permissions for both Codex and OpenCode\n- Uses Skills-style service groups with individual tool selection and tri-state\n  parent checkboxes; the title, count, whitespace and arrow only expand/collapse\n- Saves explicit tool names, so new tools are not automatically authorized\n- Preserves immutable permissions in existing conversations; Agent edits apply\n  to new conversations, and globally disabled MCP services remain blocked\n- Retains old whole-service bindings until explicitly narrowed and safely\n  handles removed tools and cross-service name collisions\n- Reuses AgentOS Runtime 1.0.0-beta.26 without rebuilding sandbox templates\n- Preserves configuration, credentials, conversations, attachments, Skills and\n  durable workspace files when upgrading\n\nValidation: 1,286 passing tests with one existing platform-specific skip before\nrelease versioning, two rounds of real Codex/OpenCode read/write permission\nchecks, and real-browser mouse/keyboard, light/dark and narrow-screen checks",
